// Animals and people as bodies, fighters and herds (old AnimalFactory, AnimalType and the herd
// behaviours). Loaded once by Content; ContentTests checks every name in here resolves.
//
// species: every Species has one row.
//   body, weightKg, fatPct, musclePct: the body plan and its average build (members vary around it).
//   role: how it meets a threat. isSmall: small game, which runs where a big one of its role would not.
//   attackDamage, attackType: its unarmed attack. threat, boldness, aggression, cohesion: the morale
//   numbers combat runs on; cohesion is also how strongly an animal sticks with its kin (Fauna).
//   group: Open counts any animal of its species on its tile as kin; Closed only those it is familiar with.
//   moveAllowanceM: metres covered in one combat action at full Moving.
//   reachM: how far from its body it strikes unarmed (research §2: jaws 0.3, a bear's paw 1.0, tusks 2.5; D
//   where the research gives none). attackDamage is on the weapons' scale (units of tissue condition), what
//   an average member's blow does: a wolf's bite does not get through a person's flesh, a spear's thrust does.
//   temperament: what makes its herd come at a target (a name in temperaments).
//   behavior: how its herd lives (old HerdBehaviorType; Opportunist: a small scavenger, neither predator nor prey). diet: what its herd grazes (a name in diets).
//   Humans and hares never form herds of their own; theirs are the old defaults, Prey and Carnivore.
//   How it runs (documentation/species-stats-research.md §5.3), fresh and unladen: topSpeedMps, flat out;
//   enduranceSpeedMps, the pace it holds for 20 minutes or more; sprintSeconds, the seconds at top speed
//   that empty a full sprint reserve; runCostJPerKgM, the net cost of running a metre (Taylor 1982, a
//   person's measured); burstPct, the share of the reserve one strike, dodge or shove takes. The reserve
//   refills over a recovery time derived from the body's weight (Body.RecoverySeconds).
//   chaseLimitSeconds: how long it runs after a fleeing quarry before giving up (Mech 1966: wolves quit
//     a moose that kept its lead for 10-15 s, unless they were gaining; D otherwise).
//   strikeBackResolve: giving ground with the enemy in reach, it strikes instead of backing off while its
//     resolve (Combat.Resolve) is at or above this (-0.3 gives ground, -0.8 runs): when to fight a retreat is the
//     tuner's to learn (decided 2026-11-21). A starting value, the same for all.
//   grazeKcalPerMinute: what a member eats a minute grazing (winter forage, research §4.1); 0 for what never grazes.
//   flightMinutesPerTile: a flyer's flat minutes a tile, over any ground and water but not the mountain wall
//     (absent for what walks). A raven: 1 (D; ravens cover 100 m in seconds).
//   sleepHoursPerDay: the hours a day it sleeps; its rest drains over the rest of the day and refills over these
//     (Body.EnergyDeltaPerMinute; a person's 8). Grazers sleep little, hunters a lot (D, from the literature's ranges).
//   activity: Diurnal, Crepuscular (dawn and dusk) or Nocturnal: its active hours. Outside them it would rather rest,
//     watches less and is warier (Fauna.ActiveNow); the spec's list, with the hare crepuscular (D).
//   perceptionFactor (optional, 1): its sight budget against a person's, for sensing what moves (Fauna.Sense).
//   stealthFactor (optional, 1): how hard a hunter of its kind is to notice coming (Fauna.PreyNotices; the old herd stealth).
//   smellFactor: its sense of smell, scaling how far it smells a scent (Scent; a nose of 1 smells a full scent
//     Scent.FullReachTiles in calm air). scentLevel: the scent its body gives off, 0-1, low for people (spec).
//     Both D: bears out-smell dogs, wolves and hyenas close behind, ravens find food by sight (R); see the
//     work log .agent-logs/2026-11-24-123-scent-carried-downwind.md.
//   People only: autumnFatPct, the range a person's starting fat is drawn from (well fed for the autumn:
//   SpeciesTable.NewBody); female, a woman's build, running and autumn fat, where they differ from a man's.
// Every number's source is tagged by its row: V read in a primary source, R recalled from the literature
// (check before pinning a test to it), D derived or judged (documentation/species-stats-research.md).
//
// temperaments: base, a bonus per member, hunger (hungryAt, starvingAt, hungerBonus), defending a kill
//   or den (defendBonus), and a ceiling (cap). Cap 0 never starts a fight.
// diets: what each Diet takes off a tile's forage, in order (old AnimalDietExtensions.GetConsumedResources).
// sightings: how watchful a stalked animal is, by what its herd is doing; one is picked at random
//   (old HuntingSightings' DetectionModifier values, pool by pool, in their order).
